  "Question": "The value of\n\n\\[\\dfrac{(0.2)^3}{(0.02)^2}\\]\n\nis",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(15\\)",
    "E": "\\(20\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Calculate the powers before dividing:\n\\[\n(0.2)^3=0.2\\times0.2\\times0.2=0.008,\n\\]\n\\[\n(0.02)^2=0.02\\times0.02=0.0004.\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive, so division is defined. Multiplying both numerator and denominator by \\(10000\\) makes the division simpler:\n\\[\n\\frac{0.008}{0.0004}=\\frac{80}{4}=20.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
